settings.local.json

# Jess's global gitexcludes ignores .tool-versions (a sensible default: tool
# pins are usually personal). Here it's the opposite — the asdf pin is the
# thing that keeps every one of Jess's computers on the same Ruby, so it has
# to be tracked. A repo .gitignore outranks core.excludesFile, so this wins.
!.tool-versions
